Riya backend — Postman test checklist
=====================================

Base URL: `http://localhost:3001/api/v1`

Create a Postman environment with these variables:

```text
baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api/v1
accessToken = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
adminAccessToken = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
productId =
variantId =
orderId =
categoryId =
```

Start the backend:

```bash
cd Riya-backend/riya-backend
npm run start:dev
```

Before testing, create `riya_local` in DBeaver and run `riya-backend/database/local/setup.sql`. It creates all tables plus local demo users, products, variants, settings and contact information.

Public requests (no Authorization header)
-----------------------------------------

### Health

`GET {{baseUrl}}/health`

Expected: `success: true`, `data.status: "ok"`.

### Categories

`GET {{baseUrl}}/categories`

Copy any `data[0].id` to `categoryId`.

### Products

`GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=20`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=gingelly`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/products?category=gingelly-oil`

Copy `data.items[0].id` to `productId` and `data.items[0].product_variants[0].id` to `variantId`.

You can use this Postman **Tests** script after the product-list request to save them automatically:

```javascript
const product = pm.response.json().data.items[0];
pm.environment.set('productId', product.id);
pm.environment.set('variantId', product.product_variants[0].id);
```

### Product detail

`GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}`

### Store and contact information

`GET {{baseUrl}}/settings`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/content/contact`

### Guest checkout

`POST {{baseUrl}}/orders`

Header: `Content-Type: application/json`

```json
{
  "items": [
    { "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 2 }
  ],
  "customer": {
    "name": "Demo Guest",
    "phone": "9876543210",
    "email": "guest@example.com"
  },
  "shippingAddress": {
    "addressLine": "12 Demo Street",
    "city": "Coimbatore",
    "district": "Coimbatore",
    "state": "Tamil Nadu",
    "pincode": "641001"
  }
}
```

Expected: the server calculates `subtotal`, `shipping_fee`, and `total`; prices supplied by a client are ignored. Save the returned order id with this Tests script:

```javascript
pm.environment.set('orderId', pm.response.json().data.id);
```

Customer requests (Bearer `{{accessToken}}`)
---------------------------------------------

During local PostgreSQL development, the Bearer value is the seeded customer UUID above. A guest order is deliberately not visible through these endpoints.

`GET {{baseUrl}}/orders`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}`

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel`

Cancellation is allowed only while an order is `PENDING` or `CONFIRMED`.

To create an order attached to the customer, repeat guest checkout with `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}`.

Admin requests (Bearer `{{adminAccessToken}}`)
----------------------------------------------

For local development, use the seeded admin UUID above. It maps to an ADMIN profile in the local database. When Supabase is enabled later, replace this local-only bearer mechanism with Supabase Auth:

```sql
update public.profiles set role = 'ADMIN' where user_id = '<auth-user-uuid>';
```

### Categories

`POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/categories`

```json
{ "name": "Demo Oils", "slug": "demo-oils", "description": "Temporary test category", "isActive": true }
```

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/categories/{{categoryId}}` — use the same body with changed values.

`DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/categories/{{categoryId}}`

### Products

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/products?page=1&limit=20`

`POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/products`

```json
{
  "name": "Postman Test Oil",
  "slug": "postman-test-oil",
  "description": "A test-only product created from Postman.",
  "shortDescription": "Test oil",
  "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}",
  "weight": "1L",
  "ingredients": "Demo ingredients",
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://placehold.co/800x800?text=Test+Oil",
  "images": ["https://placehold.co/800x800?text=Test+Oil"],
  "isFeatured": false,
  "isActive": true,
  "variants": [
    { "name": "1L", "size": 1, "unit": "L", "sku": "POSTMAN-TEST-1L", "price": 250, "salePrice": 225, "stock": 10, "isActive": true }
  ]
}
```

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}`

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}` — send the complete product body above; change only desired values.

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/variants/{{variantId}}`

```json
{ "name": "1L", "size": 1, "unit": "L", "sku": "POSTMAN-TEST-1L", "price": 250, "salePrice": 225, "stock": 25, "isActive": true }
```

`DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}`

### Orders, customers, dashboard

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders?status=PENDING&search=Demo&page=1&limit=20`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}`

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status`

```json
{ "status": "CONFIRMED", "note": "Confirmed during Postman test" }
```

Allowed normal lifecycle: `PENDING → CONFIRMED → PROCESSING → PACKED → SHIPPED → DELIVERED`. An admin can also cancel a PENDING or CONFIRMED order.

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/customers`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/customers/<customer-auth-user-id>`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/customers/<customer-auth-user-id>/orders`

`GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard/stats`

### Settings and contact content

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/settings`

```json
{ "storeName": "Riya Demo Store", "currency": "INR", "shippingFee": 50, "freeShippingThreshold": 999, "supportPhone": "9876543210", "supportEmail": "support@riya.demo" }
```

`PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/content/contact`

```json
{ "businessName": "Riya Demo Store", "phone": "9876543210", "email": "hello@riya.demo", "whatsapp": "919876543210", "address": "123 Market Road, Coimbatore", "businessHours": "Mon-Sat, 9 AM - 6 PM" }
```
